The central finding that shapes the piece: CEN's signature on the HPA axis is often *hypocortisolism* — not chronic over-activation but eventual collapse into flatness and blunted stress response — which is why neglect-affected adults so often present as exhausted and numb rather than visibly anxious. The hook is the cortisol awakening response as a literal measurable trace of emotional absence, detectable in saliva decades later. The smoke-detector metaphor (exquisitely recalibrated to a more dangerous world, still misfiring — or finally burning out) threads the piece together and connects to the somatic repair work already covered in earlier entries in this series.
